{
    "background_story": "Thaddeus was a 19th-century English aristocrat with a reputation for being a bit of an eccentric. Behind the closed doors of his opulent mansion, he harbored a secret passion for inventing and collecting peculiar devices. Thaddeus's fascination with the unconventional led him to create an array of kinky contraptions, from intricate corsets to curious mechanical toys. His love of the unusual also extended to his art collection, featuring works by the likes of Aubrey Beardsley and other avant-garde artists. Thaddeus's kinkiness wasn't just about his interests, but also about his approach to life. He believed in pushing boundaries and exploring the uncharted, often hosting lavish masquerade balls that were the talk of the town. Despite the whispers and raised eyebrows, Thaddeus remained unapologetic about his tastes, living life on his own terms.",
